From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] frontends/nss: always tell the firmware the ingress shaper
 tags of a rule

With an ingress shaper on the conduit (sqm-scripts-nss, nss-edma.qos:
act_nssmirred from the conduit to an ifb), every frame the switch hands to
the SoC passes the ifb's nssprio, and the rule of its flow says which band
it takes. ECM fills in the ingress tags of a rule only when a classifier
supplied them, and that is the DSCP classifier, from the conntrack entry.
A bridged flow has no such entry: its rule goes to the firmware without
NSS_IPV{4,6}_RULE_CREATE_IGS_VALID, and the firmware then shapes some of
those flows as WAN downloads.

Seen on a GL-B3000 (firmware 12.5) with a 150 Mbit/s ingress limit on wan:
iperf3 UDP at 500 Mbit/s from a host on lan1 to a 802.11s mesh peer on
5 GHz, both in br-lan, 16 source ports. Without this change 8 to 11 of the
16 arrive at 141 Mbit/s, with the drops counted by the WAN nsstbl on the
ifb; which ports changes after the rules are flushed. With it, 48 of 48
runs in three series arrive at 386 to 464 Mbit/s with no drop in the WAN
nsstbl, and a download from the WAN still goes through that nsstbl.

Send the tags with every unicast rule: the classifier's, or 0 when there
are none. Multicast rules are left as they are.

Link: https://github.com/kuncy7/openwrt-nss-edma/issues/69
Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
---
--- a/frontends/nss/ecm_nss_ported_ipv4.c
+++ b/frontends/nss/ecm_nss_ported_ipv4.c
@@ -1243,6 +1243,15 @@ static void ecm_nss_ported_ipv4_connecti
 		nircm->igs_rule.igs_flow_qos_tag = (uint16_t)pr->igs_flow_qos_tag;
 		nircm->igs_rule.igs_return_qos_tag = (uint16_t)pr->igs_return_qos_tag;
 		nircm->valid_flags |= NSS_IPV4_RULE_CREATE_IGS_VALID;
+	} else {
+		/*
+		 * No classifier gave ingress tags, as for a bridged flow, which
+		 * the DSCP classifier never sees. Say so: a rule that leaves the
+		 * tags out can be shaped as if it had some.
+		 */
+		nircm->igs_rule.igs_flow_qos_tag = 0;
+		nircm->igs_rule.igs_return_qos_tag = 0;
+		nircm->valid_flags |= NSS_IPV4_RULE_CREATE_IGS_VALID;
 	}
 #endif
 	/*

